{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["And it shall be if you will indeed hear — and I will give rain — (If you listened yesterday, you will listen tomorrow; and similarly, if you forgot, you will forget — if you began to forget, your end will be that you forget. Thus it is taught in the Aggadah of Shmuel; in Megillat Hasidim they found written: If you abandon Him one day, He will abandon you two. A parable: two men set out, one from Tiberias and one from Sepphoris, and they met each other at one parsang's distance. They conversed with each other and then parted; this one went a mile and that one went a mile — and they were found to be two miles apart from each other. Addition.)" "And it shall be if you will indeed hear — and I will give rain — and you shall eat and be satisfied without toil; and if not — וְעָצַר אֶת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְלֹא יִהְיֶה מָטָר."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The entire comment appears to be a later addition ('תוספת') appended to Rashbam's commentary; I have translated it as found, including the parenthetical framing and the closing tag."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:41.703474655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}